{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YJjgaNmyn9NoLBRLHWN1Ns","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd038-unlink\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/unlink: Remove a Single File\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The unlink utility provides a minimal interface to the unlink(2) system call, removing exactly\n6\t  one file without the recursive or force semantics of rm. The macOS BSD unlink and GNU unlink\n7\t  behave identically for valid inputs but differ in error message formatting. The Go implementation\n8\t  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gunlink, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n9\t  output and exit codes, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Remove exactly one file by calling the unlink(2) system call.\n13\t  - G2: Reject invalid usage with appropriate error messages and exit codes.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Basic operation\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must call unlink(2) on exactly one FILE argument provided on the command line.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: Must produce no output on stdout when the operation succeeds.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n25\t\n26\t  R2:\n27\t    title: Error handling\n28\t    items:\n29\t      - R2.1:\n30\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when called with zero arguments.\n31\t      - R2.2:\n32\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when called with more than one argument.\n33\t      - R2.3:\n34\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when the specified FILE does not exist.\n35\t      - R2.4:\n36\t          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when the specified FILE is a directory, since unlink(2) does not remove directories on standard systems.\n37\t\n38\t  R3:\n39\t    title: Differential testing\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R3.1:\n42\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and gunlink via pkg/testutils.\n43\t      - R3.2:\n44\t          text: \"Tests must cover: successful removal of a regular file, successful removal of a symbolic link, zero-argument error, multi-argument error, non-existent file error, and directory argument error.\"\n45\t      - R3.3:\n46\t          text: Tests must verify that the target file no longer exists after a successful invocation, matching gunlink behavior.\n47\t\n48\tnon_goals:\n49\t  - cmd/unlink does not support any flags; it accepts exactly one positional argument.\n50\t  - cmd/unlink does not remove directories; use rmdir for empty directories or rm -r for non-empty ones.\n51\t  - cmd/unlink does not read filenames from stdin; input comes from the command-line argument only.\n52\t\n53\tacceptance_criteria:\n54\t  - id: AC1\n55\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink testfile removes testfile and exits 0, matching gunlink.\"\n56\t    traces:\n57\t      - R1.3\n58\t      - R2.1\n59\t      - R2.2\n60\t      - R2.3\n61\t      - R2.4\n62\t      - R3.1\n63\t  - id: AC2\n64\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink (no arguments) exits non-zero with an error message, matching gunlink.\"\n65\t    traces:\n66\t      - R2.1\n67\t      - R2.2\n68\t      - R2.3\n69\t      - R2.4\n70\t      - R3.1\n71\t      - R3.2\n72\t  - id: AC3\n73\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink a b exits non-zero with an error message, matching gunlink.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R2.1\n76\t      - R2.2\n77\t      - R2.3\n78\t      - R2.4\n79\t      - R3.1\n80\t      - R3.2\n81\t  - id: AC4\n82\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink nonexistent exits non-zero with an error message, matching gunlink.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R2.3\n87\t      - R2.4\n88\t      - R3.1\n89\t      - R3.2\n90\t  - id: AC5\n91\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gunlink passes for regular file, symbolic link, zero args, multi args, non-existent, and directory cases.\"\n92\t    traces:\n93\t      - R3.1\n94\t      - R3.2\n95\t  - id: AC6\n96\t    criterion: \"cmd/unlink compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n97\t    traces:\n98\t      - R1.1\n99\t      - R1.2\n100\t      - R1.3\n101\t      - R2.1\n102\t      - R2.2\n103\t      - R2.3\n104\t      - R2.4\n105\t      - R3.1\n106\t      - R3.2\n107\t      - R3.3\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3571da7-d227-48db-ba5a-59043565034c","uuid":"af652058-48a2-4791-932a-52351597e01c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T11:06:05.097Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5335/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd038-unlink.yaml","content":"id: srd038-unlink\ntitle: \"cmd/unlink: Remove a Single File\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The unlink utility provides a minimal interface to the unlink(2) system call, removing exactly\n  one file without the recursive or force semantics of rm. The macOS BSD unlink and GNU unlink\n  behave identically for valid inputs but differ in error message formatting. The Go implementation\n  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gunlink, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on\n  output and exit codes, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Remove exactly one file by calling the unlink(2) system call.\n  - G2: Reject invalid usage with appropriate error messages and exit codes.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic operation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must call unlink(2) on exactly one FILE argument provided on the command line.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must produce no output on stdout when the operation succeeds.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when called with zero arguments.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when called with more than one argument.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when the specified FILE does not exist.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: Must exit with a non-zero status and print an error to stderr when the specified FILE is a directory, since unlink(2) does not remove directories on standard systems.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr, and exit codes between the Go binary and gunlink via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: successful removal of a regular file, successful removal of a symbolic link, zero-argument error, multi-argument error, non-existent file error, and directory argument error.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Tests must verify that the target file no longer exists after a successful invocation, matching gunlink behavior.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/unlink does not support any flags; it accepts exactly one positional argument.\n  - cmd/unlink does not remove directories; use rmdir for empty directories or rm -r for non-empty ones.\n  - cmd/unlink does not read filenames from stdin; input comes from the command-line argument only.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink testfile removes testfile and exits 0, matching gunlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink (no arguments) exits non-zero with an error message, matching gunlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink a b exits non-zero with an error message, matching gunlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/unlink nonexistent exits non-zero with an error message, matching gunlink.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gunlink passes for regular file, symbolic link, zero args, multi args, non-existent, and directory cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/unlink compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":108,"startLine":1,"totalLines":108}}}
