{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011kx1oebWCpjtsckG8RGvCg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - the directory case is different. On macOS, `os.Remove()` can actually remove empty directories (it calls `unlink()` first, and if that fails, tries `rmdir()`). But `gunlink` specifically calls `unlink(2)` which fails on directories. Let me check Go's `os.Remove` source - it tries unlink first and then rmdir. So for a directory, `os.Remove` will successfully remove it via rmdir, while `unlink(2)` (which gunlink uses) fails.\n\nI need to use `syscall.Unlink()` directly instead of `os.Remove()` to match the exact behavior of the unlink(2) system call. \n\nThe requirement R1.1 explicitly says \"Must call unlink(2)\" - using `os.Remove` doesn't satisfy that since it has fallback rmdir behavior. I should switch to `syscall.Unlink()` to ensure I'm calling the actual unlink(2) system call.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":35311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3571da7-d227-48db-ba5a-59043565034c","uuid":"95c249bf-80aa-4c1c-ab31-27f649a96fa9"}
